    {
      "id": "r20261022-a02",
      "title": "Why We Forget Things",
      "level": "Menengah atas",
      "min": 4,
      "body": [
        "Everyone forgets things. You walk into a room and cannot remember why. You meet someone new and forget their name a minute later. Scientists say this is completely normal, and in some ways it is actually useful.",
        "Our brains receive huge amounts of information every day. If we remembered everything, our minds would be full of useless details. Forgetting is how the brain cleans itself. It removes information that we do not need, so important memories can stay clear.",
        "However, we can remember important things better with a few simple habits. Sleep well, because the brain organizes memories during sleep. Repeat new information several times. And connect new facts to things you already know. Forgetting will always be part of life, but you can choose what stays."
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "huge": "sangat besar",
        "useless": "tidak berguna",
        "removes": "menghapus",
        "clear": "jelas",
        "habits": "kebiasaan",
        "organizes": "mengatur"
      },
